      "text": "Section 1.482-1(f) provides a cross-reference coordination rule directing that the arm's length standards and general principles established under § 1.482-1 are to be read in conjunction with the specific methods applicable to transfers of intangible property set out in § 1.482-4. This provision ensures that the foundational arm's length framework — including comparability analysis, best method selection, and arm's length range concepts — governs the application of intangible property transfer pricing methods. The coordination rule signals that § 1.482-4 methods (comparable uncontrolled transaction, comparable profits method, profit split, and unspecified methods) operate within, and do not supersede, the overarching standards of § 1.482-1. Taxpayers determining taxable income in connection with a transfer of intangible property must therefore satisfy both the general arm's length requirements of § 1.482-1 and the specific methodological requirements of § 1.482-4.",
