      "frameworkId": "irc-482",
      "citation": "§ 1.482-1(i)",
      "title": "Scope and Consistency Principles for IRC § 482 Allocations",
      "text": "Section 1.482-1(i) establishes foundational principles governing the application of § 482 allocations. The provision addresses three core areas: (i) general principles applicable to all § 482 determinations, including the authority of the Commissioner to make allocations between or among controlled taxpayers to clearly reflect income; (ii) consistency in accounting, requiring that the methods and accounting practices used to compute the results of controlled transactions be applied consistently across controlled and uncontrolled transactions so that meaningful comparisons can be made — taxpayers may not selectively adopt accounting treatments that distort the arm's length result; and (iii) allocations between the relevant business activity and other activities, addressing the need to properly identify and separate the income, costs, and assets attributable to the controlled transaction or business activity under examination from those attributable to other activities of the controlled taxpayer. Together these principles ensure that § 482 adjustments are based on a coherent, internally consistent analytical framework and that the taxpayer's accounting practices do not introduce artificial distortions that undermine comparability or obscure the arm's length standard. These principles align with OECD Transfer Pricing Guidelines Chapter I guidance on delineating the actual transaction and ensuring consistency in the application of transfer pricing methods.",
