      "id": "irc482-1d",
      "frameworkId": "irc-482",
      "citation": "§ 1.482-1(d)",
      "title": "Section 482 Transfer Pricing — General Definitions",
      "text": "§ 1.482-1(d) sets forth the definitions applicable to the arm's length standard and controlled transaction analysis under IRC § 482. Key defined terms include: 'controlled' and 'controlled taxpayer' (any one of two or more taxpayers owned or controlled directly or indirectly by the same interests, including the taxpayer that owns or controls the other taxpayers); 'uncontrolled' and 'uncontrolled taxpayer' (any taxpayer other than a controlled taxpayer); 'controlled transaction' (any transaction between or among members of the same group of controlled taxpayers); 'uncontrolled transaction' (any transaction between taxpayers that are not members of the same controlled group); 'arm's length result' (the result that would have been realized if uncontrolled taxpayers had engaged in the same transaction under the same circumstances); and 'true taxable income' (the taxable income a controlled taxpayer would have reported had it dealt at arm's length with its controlled counterparties). These definitions establish the conceptual boundary between related-party and third-party transactions, and define the population of transactions subject to reallocation under § 482. The definitions are foundational to the comparability analysis required by the arm's length standard, aligning with OECD Transfer Pricing Guidelines Chapter I concepts of 'associated enterprises' and 'controlled transactions.'",
