      "title": "Coordination of Intercompany Loan Rules with Intangible Property Transfer Pricing Methods",
      "text": "Section 1.482-2(f) provides a coordination rule directing that transfers involving intangible property are governed by the methods set forth in § 1.482-4 (Methods to determine taxable income in connection with a transfer of intangible property), rather than the general intercompany pricing rules of § 1.482-2. This provision ensures that where a transaction involves intangible property — including licenses, royalties, or transfers of intellectual property rights — the specialized intangible property methods under § 1.482-4 take precedence. The coordination rule prevents overlap and potential conflict between the general pricing rules applicable to loans and services and the more specific intangible property framework, which includes methods such as the Comparable Uncontrolled Transaction (CUT) method, the Comparable Profits Method (CPM), and the Profit Split Method. By directing taxpayers and examiners to § 1.482-4, this provision reinforces the principle that intangible property transactions require dedicated analysis under rules specifically designed to address the unique valuation challenges associated with hard-to-value intangibles, consistent with OECD Transfer Pricing Guidelines Chapters VI and VII regarding special considerations for intangibles and intra-group services.",
