      "frameworkId": "irc-482",
      "citation": "§ 1.482-2(a)",
      "title": "Section 482 General Rule — Arm's Length Standard for Controlled Transactions",
      "text": "Section 1.482-2(a) establishes the general authority of the Commissioner to allocate gross income, deductions, credits, or allowances between or among two or more organizations, trades, or businesses owned or controlled directly or indirectly by the same interests, where necessary to prevent evasion of taxes or to clearly reflect the income of any such organizations, trades, or businesses. The standard applied is the arm's length standard, which requires that the results of a controlled transaction be consistent with the results that would have been realized if uncontrolled taxpayers had engaged in the same transaction under the same circumstances. This general rule applies to all categories of controlled transactions involving transfers of money, property, or the performance of services, and provides the foundational basis for the specific methods and rules set forth in §§ 1.482-3 through 1.482-9. Where a controlled transaction does not produce arm's length results, the Commissioner may make allocations to reflect the true taxable income of the controlled taxpayer, notwithstanding the form in which the transaction was cast.",
